From 2868f93ce55ceff151455c289ee17dc49cd0b7b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Timothy B. Terriberry" <tterribe@xiph.org>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 15:18:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [encode] Cap base_setting delta.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The requested quality-or-bitrate is specified in double precision,
 but the fractional delta between mapping levels was computed in
 single precision, leaving the possibility that rounding would
 produce a delta of exactly 1.0F.
This could promote mapping j to j+1, which causes problems when j
 is already the last defined mapping for a particular setup
 template.
Instead, cap the delta at 1-FLT_EPSILON.
This ensures that the resulting (double-precision) base_setting
 remains smaller than j+1.

We could have chosen a cap of 0.999, to match the cap of j-0.001
 imposed when the requested quality exceeds the maximum of any
 mapping in the template, but this would introduce a step
 discontinuity at the boundary of each mapping point where there was
 not one before.
1-FLT_EPSILON is the smallest value distinct from 1.0F that could
 have been reached by the old code, so this should not add any new
 discontinuities.

Thanks to Tamás Zolnai for the report.

Fixes #2358
---
 lib/vorbisenc.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/vorbisenc.c b/lib/vorbisenc.c
index cf3806a6e..34f34898c 100644
--- a/lib/vorbisenc.c
+++ b/lib/vorbisenc.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <math.h>
+#include <float.h>
 
 #include "vorbis/codec.h"
 #include "vorbis/vorbisenc.h"
@@ -658,7 +659,8 @@ static const void *get_setup_template(long ch,long srate,
           float low=map[j];
           float high=map[j+1];
           float del=(req-low)/(high-low);
-          *base_setting=j+del;
+          if(del>1-FLT_EPSILON)del=1-FLT_EPSILON;
+          *base_setting=j+(double)del;
         }
 
         return(setup_list[i]);
